# Session log — 25/26 September 2026

Phases B (finished), C and D, plus the first mouse control. Details of each step are in day011–day014.log; this is the overview of the whole session.

## What was done

**Phase B wrap-up (measuring).** Diagnostics line (D key, [Debug] ShowFPS) and timing log (timing.csv, [Debug] TimingLog). Delivery safety net: queued thread results are picked up by a 50 ms timer (TMView.PumpDeliveries), after "image name shown but picture never came" after fast scrolling.

**Phase C (preloading).**
- Own JPEG decoder on pasjpeg (uJpegDecoder): really cancellable (the FPC reader's progress hook is an empty "ToDo"), rows straight into the bitmap, DCT scaling 1/2..1/8 for the quick view.
- Quick view (Screen quality) first, full image later without resetting the view.
- Wanted set: current, preload ahead/behind across folders (TNavigator.FilesAhead), several decode threads with one kept free for the current image, promote-don't-restart.
- Cache by quality, eviction by distance from the current image, automatic size (25 % of RAM).
- I/O gate: the folder scanner waits while the current image's file is read.
- EXIF orientation (uExifOrientation + 8 test pictures, TestExif: 20 checks).
- Quick view made to fit the window exactly on the worker (uImageScaling: box average + final linear step): paint of a quick view 340 ms -> 4 ms.
- Full size only after 0.7 s on an image or at once on zoom (RefineDelayMs).
- WIC (Windows Imaging Component) for full-size JPEGs (uWicDecoder), own decoder as fallback.

**Phase D (GPU).** TGLRenderer / TGLMediaView (LazOpenGLContext): tiled textures (2048, 1-pixel overlap), mipmaps, nearest from 400 %, pixels straight from the BGRABitmap, stepwise upload with the screen copy shown first, text bars as textures, fallback to the CPU renderer with the reason in the D line, textures restored after the window is recreated. Shared view model (TRenderer): zoom at a point, pan, free rotation angle, fit of the turned bounding box.

**Mouse control (interim default profile, uInputHandler).** Wheel = browse; X1 = zoom mode on/off, X2 = rotate mode on/off (wheel: zoom at the mouse / 5° per notch, 1° with Shift); left drag = pan; double-click = fit <-> 100 % at the point clicked; Z / R / L keys; Esc leaves a mode. All through commands with values (TCommandArgs), ready for the mouse language.

**Debugging aid.** Context menu "Save current image (debugging)": the decoded image (PNG, background thread) and a picture of the window (GPU: read back from the frame) into [Debug] SaveImageDirectory (default ..\test\saved_images\). Checked: both files correct (colours, row order, rotation, 695 %, nearest filtering). Claude can read this folder: direct feedback from now on.

